  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> undergoes a thermodynamic process in which the temperature and pressure of the gas are related as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> = constant. The molar heat capacity of the gas during the process is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
